# TranEverything

**A modular localization framework for World of Warcraft addons.**

TranEverything is an open-source project aiming to make World of Warcraft addons more accessible across different languages, without modifying the original addon files.

The project is currently in the **early planning and research stage**.

## Project Goals

- **Existing Localization Support** — Activate language resources already included in compatible addons.
- **Non-Destructive Localization** — Keep additional translations and compatibility adapters separate from original addon files.
- **Per-Addon Configuration** — Allow users to manage language preferences for individual addons where technically supported.
- **Community Language Packs** — Support independently maintained language packs distributed through GitHub repositories.
- **Diagnostics & Compatibility** — Provide tools for identifying localization conflicts and troubleshooting addon issues.
- **Future AI-Assisted Translation** — Explore AI-assisted translation after reliable addon framework detection and language resource integration are established.

## Initial Compatibility

The first development target is **World of Warcraft 3.3.5a (Build 12340)**, with initial research focused on AceLocale-based addons.

Support for additional WoW versions and localization frameworks may be introduced later.

## Planned Architecture

```text
TranEverything/
├── Core/
├── Locales/
├── Adapters/
├── Sources/
├── Diagnostics/
└── UI/
```

Community translations will be stored separately from the original addons, with the goal of minimizing runtime overhead and preserving addon compatibility.

## Development Status

**Status: Planning / Proof of Concept**

TranEverything is not yet available for general use. Features, architecture, and compatibility are subject to change as development progresses.

## Community & Contributions

The project aims to support an open ecosystem where translators and developers can maintain and distribute their own language packs without needing direct access to the core repository.

Contribution guidelines and language pack specifications will be published as the project develops.

## License

License information will be added before the first public release.

